The test passes `_desolve` an `Equality` for `y(x)`. In `_desolve`, an `Equality` is rewritten as `lhs - rhs`, and `_preprocess` identifies the function as `y(x)`. Since the call uses `hint="default"` with `type="ode"`, `_desolve` calls `classify_ode`, which sets `order` from `ode_order(eq, y(x))`; this equation contains `y''`, so the order is `2`. For default solving, `classify_ode` returns the first matching hint, and `allhints` starts with `"factorable"`, which is a valid ODE solver in `solver_map`, so `_desolve` recurses with `hint="factorable"`. On that path, `_desolve` assigns `hints["hint"] = hint` and then adds `func`, so the returned dictionary has `hint = "factorable"`, `order = 2`, and `func = y(x)`.

## Answer
{"func":"y(x)","hint":"factorable","order":2}
